<title>USA: Fortress Group Q4 net rises.</title>
<headline>Fortress Group Q4 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA, Va. 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands except per share amounts, unaudited)</p>
<p>						     Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							   December 31,</p>
<p>						   1996		 1995</p>
<p>						  Actual     Pro-forma(A)</p>
<p>  Net revenues			  $   91,409	 $   64,212</p>
<p>  Cost of sales			     77,455	     51,947</p>
<p>    Gross profit			    13,954	     12,265</p>
<p>  Selling, general and administrative  8,534		7,806</p>
<p>expense</p>
<p>    Operating income			 5,420		4,459</p>
<p>  Other income, net			    195		   77</p>
<p>    Income before provision for	  5,615		4,536</p>
<p>income taxes</p>
<p>  Provision for income taxes	     2,112		1,723</p>
<p>    Net income				 3,503		2,813</p>
<p>  Net income per share:		     0.30		 0.30</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>    outstanding			 11,731,470	  9,413,181</p>
<p>						    Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>							   December 31,</p>
<p>						   1996		 1995</p>
<p>					  Pro-forma(A)     Pro-forma(A)</p>
<p>  Net revenues			   $ 289,571	 $  199,029</p>
<p>  Cost of sales			    242,210	    164,134</p>
<p>    Gross profit			    47,361	     34,895</p>
<p>Selling, general and administrative</p>
<p>						  30,474	     24,647</p>
<p>expense</p>
<p>    Operating Income			16,887	     10,248</p>
<p>  Other income, net			    729		   55</p>
<p>    Income before provision for	 17,616	     10,303</p>
<p>income taxes</p>
<p>  Provision for income taxes	     6,700		3,915</p>
<p>    Net income				10,916		6,388</p>
<p>    Net income per share:		   1.00		 0.68</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>    outstanding			 10,819,988	  9,413,181</p>
<p>(A) Pro-forma data reflect adjustments for the acquisitions including:</p>
<p>i) Reduction in the Company's interest costs due to the Company's Initial Public Offering and Senior Note Offering in May 1996.</p>
<p>ii) Compensation differentials to former owners and employees of the combined predecessor companies.</p>
<p>iii) Incremental selling, general, and administrative expenses associated with Fortress's corporate activities.</p>
<p>iv) Income taxes as if the entities were combined and subject to the effective federal and state statutory rates throughout the periods disclosed.</p>
<p>v) Twelve-month 1996 pro-forma data reflect the sale of The Genesee Company's Custom Home division in July, 1996.</p>
<p>vi) Twelve-month 1996 pro-forma data reflect the acquisition of Landmark Homes in August 1996.</p>
<p>(B) New orders represent total new orders received during the period, net of cancellations.</p>
<p>(C) Backlog includes sales orders which have not yet closed.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
